Compliance & Licensing
======================

This engine package ("webnovel writer for LxChat") is an independent integration and
is provided under this notice:

1. webnovel-writer (the upstream project)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Project : https://github.com/lingfengQAQ/webnovel-writer
   License : GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)
   Upstream source: https://github.com/lingfengQAQ/webnovel-writer

   The upstream webnovel-writer source tree is bundled in this package UNMODIFIED
   and is invoked purely as an independent external process (aggregation), NOT
   merged into or linked statically with the LxChat codebase. Accordingly, using
   this engine does not convert the MIT-licensed LxChat app into a GPL-licensed
   work. The GPL obligations apply only to redistributions/modifications of the
   upstream webnovel-writer code itself.

   The full GPL-3.0 license text is available at:
     https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

2. The adapter (scripts/adapter.py)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   The thin adapter bridging LxChat and webnovel-writer is ORIGINAL code written
   for LxChat and is licensed under the MIT license (see the LICENSE below / this
   notice's MIT terms). It does not modify, embed, or inline GPL source; it only
   launches the upstream CLI as a subprocess and exchanges structured JSON.

3. Distribution of source
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   To comply with GPL-3.0 Section 5 (Conveying unmodified source), the upstream
   webnovel-writer source for the version shipped in this package is made available
   at the upstream repository (https://github.com/lingfengQAQ/webnovel-writer) and,
   if you redistribute this engine package, the corresponding source must be offered
   alongside or via the sourceUrl link above.

